1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:07,000
Threatened by a ruthless demon, humanity was on the brink of destruction.

2
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:16,000
All seemed lost until a lone mage stepped forward and took up the fight.

3
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:29,000
After his triumph, he was hailed as the Wizard King, and his story became legend.

4
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:35,000
Metaplon

5
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:36,000
Why?

6
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:43,400
When I 대 Village

7
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:49,000
If anybody living with my eyes, I'm realized at a moment.

8
00:00:49,500 --> 00:00:52,000
By feeling BIBLE

9
00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:56,000
Guess what'sOMSIFE?

10
00:00:56,000 --> 00:01:25,980
Thank you.

11
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:55,980
Thank you.

12
00:01:56,000 --> 00:01:58,000
Thank you.

13
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:26,760
Yeah, that's all.

14
00:02:27,160 --> 00:02:29,680
Hate to tell you, but I think they call that worrying.

15
00:02:29,860 --> 00:02:31,020
Checking up on me, huh?

16
00:02:31,360 --> 00:02:32,120
Thanks, Noelle.

17
00:02:33,120 --> 00:02:35,420
I was worried about you, too.

18
00:02:35,560 --> 00:02:37,000
I'm glad I'll create you made it back.

19
00:02:37,160 --> 00:02:39,160
Well, you obviously needed the rest.

20
00:02:39,360 --> 00:02:43,440
You know, conquering a dungeon and getting a major wound in the gut will really take it out of a guy.

21
00:02:43,660 --> 00:02:45,860
I still think a whole week is a little excessive.

22
00:02:46,280 --> 00:02:47,920
Enough of this boring chit-chat.

23
00:02:48,540 --> 00:02:49,740
Think of my goddess Marie.

24
00:02:50,200 --> 00:02:52,360
Would she enjoy such dull conversation?

25
00:02:52,940 --> 00:02:53,980
Not one bit.

26
00:02:54,120 --> 00:02:55,940
I need something interesting to tell her.

27
00:02:56,280 --> 00:02:56,940
Like a story.

28
00:02:57,300 --> 00:02:59,540
I only have 3,210 left.

29
00:02:59,560 --> 00:03:01,640
And that's not enough to tide her over for a while?

30
00:03:01,820 --> 00:03:03,640
How many stories does one girl need?

31
00:03:03,840 --> 00:03:04,800
So, how are you?

32
00:03:05,040 --> 00:03:06,580
That stomach wound all healed up now?

33
00:03:07,060 --> 00:03:08,340
Are you ready to take me on?

34
00:03:08,460 --> 00:03:09,100
Can we fight?

35
00:03:09,100 --> 00:03:11,360
I don't think it's completely healed yet.

36
00:03:11,520 --> 00:03:14,540
Although, maybe I'm just really hungry.

37
00:03:15,040 --> 00:03:16,060
Hey, everybody!

38
00:03:16,460 --> 00:03:19,620
Hope you brought your apple spice because the sheep cook's breakfast is ready!

39
00:03:19,800 --> 00:03:20,680
Oh, wow!

40
00:03:20,920 --> 00:03:21,880
This is delicious!

41
00:03:23,360 --> 00:03:24,720
Will you slow down?

42
00:03:24,760 --> 00:03:25,520
That's disgusting.

43
00:03:26,480 --> 00:03:27,560
I'm...

44
00:03:27,560 --> 00:03:33,380
Honestly, you are such a pig.

45
00:03:33,660 --> 00:03:34,360
Hey, now.

46
00:03:34,580 --> 00:03:36,480
The kiddo needs his sustenance to recover.

47
00:03:36,940 --> 00:03:37,980
Wine to wash it down?

48
00:03:37,980 --> 00:03:39,400
Sure, because that'll help.

49
00:03:40,280 --> 00:03:41,400
So good!

50
00:03:41,780 --> 00:03:42,280
That's it!

51
00:03:42,360 --> 00:03:43,060
Don't be shy!

52
00:03:43,220 --> 00:03:44,780
Show him how it's done, I'll stop!

53
00:03:45,180 --> 00:03:47,560
The sheep cooks love a guy who knows how to eat!

54
00:03:50,960 --> 00:03:53,480
Gonna grab some chow, then it's back to bed.

55
00:03:53,840 --> 00:03:55,180
Oh, hey, Captain Yummy!

56
00:03:55,500 --> 00:03:56,180
Good morning!

57
00:03:56,500 --> 00:03:58,220
Good morning, Captain Yummy, sir!

58
00:03:58,420 --> 00:04:00,440
So, kid, looks like you finally woke up.

59
00:04:00,760 --> 00:04:02,060
Didn't die after all.

60
00:04:02,420 --> 00:04:02,720
Nope!

61
00:04:02,720 --> 00:04:03,760
Still alive, sir!

62
00:04:05,820 --> 00:04:07,320
Well, good job out there.

63
00:04:07,320 --> 00:04:09,520
Even if you did get yourself wrecked again.

64
00:04:10,620 --> 00:04:11,520
Thank you, sir!

65
00:04:12,020 --> 00:04:12,400
Right.

66
00:04:12,660 --> 00:04:16,480
Now then, Knight's Headquarters wants a report on the dungeon ASAP.

67
00:04:17,400 --> 00:04:19,020
So if you can walk, you're going.

68
00:04:19,620 --> 00:04:19,840
What?

69
00:04:20,240 --> 00:04:20,900
A report?

70
00:04:21,580 --> 00:04:22,940
Oh, at Knight's Headquarters?

71
00:04:22,940 --> 00:04:25,820
I bet there are tons of tough guys there.

72
00:04:26,120 --> 00:04:27,460
Wonder how many I can fight!

73
00:04:27,940 --> 00:04:30,340
I know that look on your face, and it means trouble.

74
00:04:30,700 --> 00:04:31,660
No way you're going.

75
00:04:31,820 --> 00:04:32,360
Aw!

76
00:04:33,320 --> 00:04:36,900
I'm sending you out on a battle mission instead with Magna Babysitter.

77
00:04:37,140 --> 00:04:38,200
A battle mission?

78
00:04:38,740 --> 00:04:40,740
We'll make a great team, right, Magna?

79
00:04:40,740 --> 00:04:42,740
Uh, what's with you?

80
00:04:42,900 --> 00:04:44,720
How can I be sure you're really luck?

81
00:04:45,060 --> 00:04:46,660
You could be gray in disguise.

82
00:04:47,160 --> 00:04:47,500
Sure.

83
00:04:48,300 --> 00:04:48,960
Never mind!

84
00:04:49,400 --> 00:04:50,320
Hey, sir!

85
00:04:50,860 --> 00:04:51,700
You can send me.

86
00:04:51,800 --> 00:04:52,660
I don't mind going.

87
00:04:52,860 --> 00:04:53,180
Really?

88
00:04:53,620 --> 00:04:55,440
Just think of all the delectively done

89
00:04:55,440 --> 00:04:57,440
going to chase the noble robot to offer!

90
00:04:57,820 --> 00:04:59,040
They'll take this the wrong way,

91
00:04:59,080 --> 00:05:00,520
but why the heck would I send you?

92
00:05:00,820 --> 00:05:02,620
All you do is sit around eating all day.

93
00:05:03,080 --> 00:05:03,440
What?

94
00:05:03,440 --> 00:05:07,660
Captain, sir.

95
00:05:08,060 --> 00:05:09,480
I'm sorry, but I can't go.

96
00:05:09,840 --> 00:05:11,460
I'm busy writing letters to Marie.

97
00:05:11,960 --> 00:05:12,400
Okay.

98
00:05:12,840 --> 00:05:15,460
It's not like anyone asked you to go anyway.

99
00:05:15,460 --> 00:05:16,960
I'm a good one, huh?

100
00:05:21,480 --> 00:05:22,040
Whoa!

101
00:05:24,600 --> 00:05:25,520
This is awesome!

102
00:05:26,020 --> 00:05:28,940
I mean, I knew it was big, but up close it's huge!

103
00:05:29,940 --> 00:05:31,340
Keep it down, would you?

104
00:05:31,640 --> 00:05:33,680
You're embarrassing both of us right now.

105
00:05:34,020 --> 00:05:35,000
So cool!

106
00:05:35,800 --> 00:05:36,780
Stop yelling!

107
00:05:39,000 --> 00:05:40,100
We're alone again.

108
00:05:40,460 --> 00:05:41,480
Just me and him.

109
00:05:44,060 --> 00:05:44,540
Enormous.

110
00:05:45,620 --> 00:05:46,100
Gigantic.

111
00:05:46,120 --> 00:05:47,700
Are you still going on about that?

112
00:05:47,880 --> 00:05:49,520
It's not all that special, you know.

113
00:05:50,120 --> 00:05:51,140
Oh, it's them.

114
00:05:51,540 --> 00:05:53,880
Why, if it isn't the members of the Golden Dawn!

115
00:05:54,000 --> 00:05:54,760
Hello there!

116
00:05:55,120 --> 00:05:57,700
Hey, we haven't seen you since the dungeon, Asta.

117
00:05:57,940 --> 00:05:59,900
I assume you've come to make your report, too?

118
00:05:59,900 --> 00:06:02,480
Is your wound all healed up?

119
00:06:02,920 --> 00:06:03,240
Yeah!

120
00:06:03,680 --> 00:06:07,740
My stomach still hurts a bit, but after lots of food and sleep, I bounce back.

121
00:06:07,940 --> 00:06:08,740
Such a child.

122
00:06:09,340 --> 00:06:10,660
Who's a child here?

123
00:06:10,760 --> 00:06:11,060
You.

124
00:06:11,400 --> 00:06:13,020
You're the same age as me, you know!

125
00:06:15,020 --> 00:06:16,940
Hey, I really owe you one, Mimosa.

126
00:06:17,300 --> 00:06:18,720
Thanks so much for patching me up!

127
00:06:21,520 --> 00:06:22,240
What's wrong?

128
00:06:22,300 --> 00:06:23,060
Why'd she run away?

129
00:06:23,060 --> 00:06:27,720
She was probably shocked to see how much shorter your arm is than she imagined it would be.

130
00:06:28,220 --> 00:06:28,620
So.

131
00:06:29,060 --> 00:06:31,560
And what the hell's that supposed to mean, huh?!

132
00:06:31,560 --> 00:06:32,000
So.

133
00:06:32,900 --> 00:06:33,380
Seriously!

134
00:06:33,860 --> 00:06:34,480
Just give up.

135
00:06:34,820 --> 00:06:35,940
What's wrong, Mimosa?

136
00:06:38,340 --> 00:06:39,180
You alright?

137
00:06:40,180 --> 00:06:41,420
I don't know what to do!

138
00:06:41,680 --> 00:06:42,660
Please help me!

139
00:06:43,320 --> 00:06:44,880
It's, um, Asta.

140
00:06:45,600 --> 00:06:48,400
Whenever I see him, I get this weird feeling in my chest.

141
00:06:48,740 --> 00:06:51,880
Since that day in the dungeon, he's all I can ever seem to think about.

142
00:06:52,780 --> 00:06:53,660
It's awful!

143
00:06:54,420 --> 00:06:56,200
I don't know what's gotten into me!

144
00:06:56,200 --> 00:06:59,880
Is that the way I just ran from him?

145
00:07:00,180 --> 00:07:02,040
Do you think he's going to hate me now?

146
00:07:03,160 --> 00:07:05,100
What can you possibly see in him?

147
00:07:05,420 --> 00:07:07,940
He's a low-born, little-brained, loud-mouthed runt!

148
00:07:09,180 --> 00:07:12,100
I think those things are all just part of his charm, honestly.

149
00:07:12,520 --> 00:07:14,880
So much life in such a compact package.

150
00:07:16,160 --> 00:07:17,860
Could this be...

151
00:07:17,860 --> 00:07:19,580
No, no, no!

152
00:07:19,740 --> 00:07:21,120
Not that muscle-bound freak!

153
00:07:22,180 --> 00:07:23,040
Please, hold on.

154
00:07:23,360 --> 00:07:25,140
Why am I so worked up about this?

155
00:07:25,540 --> 00:07:25,860
No.

156
00:07:26,200 --> 00:07:27,220
Not a chance!

157
00:07:27,620 --> 00:07:28,160
Me and him?

158
00:07:28,560 --> 00:07:28,900
Never!

159
00:07:32,940 --> 00:07:34,280
What's all the moaning about?

160
00:07:34,960 --> 00:07:35,260
Hmm.

161
00:07:35,740 --> 00:07:37,020
Maybe their heads are hurting?

162
00:07:39,080 --> 00:07:41,340
Knight's headquarters ought to be just through here.

163
00:07:42,200 --> 00:07:44,920
Guess there are some things even you don't know, huh, Four Eyes?

164
00:07:44,940 --> 00:07:47,020
Even we Four Eyes can't know everything.

165
00:07:47,720 --> 00:07:50,560
I guess somewhere along the line he accepted his new nickname.

166
00:07:51,280 --> 00:07:53,620
Wow, look how much better he's treating Asta.

167
00:07:54,060 --> 00:07:54,480
Anyway,

168
00:07:54,480 --> 00:07:56,720
we don't often come to headquarters,

169
00:07:56,720 --> 00:07:57,980
so it's easy to forget.

170
00:08:02,560 --> 00:08:03,000
No!

171
00:08:03,540 --> 00:08:04,940
Is that really...

172
00:08:04,940 --> 00:08:07,260
I never dreamed you would greet us personally, sir.

173
00:08:07,260 --> 00:08:13,340
He's flashy.

174
00:08:13,340 --> 00:08:15,000
Who do you think this guy is?

175
00:08:15,440 --> 00:08:16,320
You idiot!

176
00:08:16,920 --> 00:08:19,220
This is none other than the current Wizard King,

177
00:08:19,460 --> 00:08:21,160
Sir Julius Novachrono.

178
00:08:21,160 --> 00:08:27,300
It's actually him.

179
00:08:27,300 --> 00:08:28,780
The Wizard King!

180
00:08:28,780 --> 00:08:48,720
I'm pleased you were able to obtain this.

181
00:08:48,720 --> 00:08:50,740
This magic is very powerful.

182
00:08:50,740 --> 00:08:53,460
It could easily be that dungeon's greatest relic.

183
00:08:53,560 --> 00:08:54,900
You can really read it, sir?

184
00:08:55,120 --> 00:08:56,240
A little of it, yes.

185
00:08:56,520 --> 00:08:57,980
The greatest relic in there?

186
00:08:58,320 --> 00:08:59,100
Go us!

187
00:09:00,100 --> 00:09:01,720
Hmm, let's see here.

188
00:09:04,200 --> 00:09:05,240
Such excitement!

189
00:09:05,240 --> 00:09:10,160
So the rumors of the Wizard King being an unparalleled magic geek were true.

190
00:09:10,820 --> 00:09:11,560
What do you say?

191
00:09:12,060 --> 00:09:14,180
Will you cast this spell for me, pretty please?

192
00:09:14,380 --> 00:09:15,480
I'd love to see it!

193
00:09:16,300 --> 00:09:17,420
I'm sorry, sir.

194
00:09:17,900 --> 00:09:20,660
I believe it somehow activated once while we were in the dungeon.

195
00:09:20,660 --> 00:09:23,040
But I haven't been able to use it again.

196
00:09:24,680 --> 00:09:26,760
Oh, I see.

197
00:09:27,300 --> 00:09:28,860
Well, too bad.

198
00:09:31,520 --> 00:09:33,160
Sylph, Spirit of Wind.

199
00:09:33,720 --> 00:09:35,360
One of the four major elements.

200
00:09:36,420 --> 00:09:38,820
So he's the one she's chosen for this era.

201
00:09:40,580 --> 00:09:42,220
I'm glad that you found this.

202
00:09:42,540 --> 00:09:45,680
All I can tell you now is that this spell will grow as you do.

203
00:09:45,920 --> 00:09:47,980
I believe it will be a tremendous help to you someday.

204
00:09:47,980 --> 00:09:52,080
Okay, make sure you take good care of her, sir.

205
00:09:52,620 --> 00:09:53,800
Wizard King, sir!

206
00:09:54,180 --> 00:09:56,560
Some weird writing showed up in my Grim War, too!

207
00:09:56,820 --> 00:09:57,740
Please take a look!

208
00:09:58,220 --> 00:09:59,400
Don't be impertinent!

209
00:10:00,560 --> 00:10:02,740
Hmm, this looks like...

210
00:10:02,740 --> 00:10:03,400
Like what?

211
00:10:04,240 --> 00:10:05,780
Something I can't read.

212
00:10:07,240 --> 00:10:07,840
Huh.

213
00:10:08,620 --> 00:10:10,680
I've never seen writing like that anywhere.

214
00:10:12,600 --> 00:10:14,180
And this comes out of it!

215
00:10:14,500 --> 00:10:15,560
What do you think, sir?

216
00:10:16,180 --> 00:10:16,680
Oh.

217
00:10:16,680 --> 00:10:18,940
A second anti-magic sword.

218
00:10:19,020 --> 00:10:19,700
That's excellent.

219
00:10:21,960 --> 00:10:23,440
Mine's working just fine.

220
00:10:24,220 --> 00:10:26,000
The power of anti-magic.

221
00:10:26,520 --> 00:10:27,220
May I...

222
00:10:27,220 --> 00:10:28,560
Do you think I could hold it?

223
00:10:29,200 --> 00:10:30,080
Go for it!

224
00:10:30,940 --> 00:10:32,200
Thank you so...

225
00:10:32,200 --> 00:10:32,500
Whoa!

226
00:10:32,660 --> 00:10:33,180
Man!

227
00:10:33,380 --> 00:10:34,740
Are you okay, Wizard King?

228
00:10:35,020 --> 00:10:37,220
I'm amazed you can swing this thing around.

229
00:10:37,220 --> 00:10:41,000
My magic power!

230
00:10:41,000 --> 00:10:42,820
It's being sucked away!

231
00:10:45,400 --> 00:10:46,600
Now I understand.

232
00:10:47,100 --> 00:10:48,520
Thanks for letting me take a look.

233
00:10:48,680 --> 00:10:49,260
Here you go.

234
00:10:49,260 --> 00:10:52,740
I think you'd better hold on to it.

235
00:10:53,240 --> 00:10:54,600
You may be the only one who can.

236
00:10:54,940 --> 00:10:58,760
It's too much for me to handle, but you can wield it because you have no magic power.

237
00:10:59,120 --> 00:11:00,000
I don't understand.

238
00:11:00,260 --> 00:11:01,840
How do you know that I don't have any magic?

239
00:11:02,300 --> 00:11:04,040
And about what my sword can do?

240
00:11:04,420 --> 00:11:07,440
Well, you know, that's an excellent question.

241
00:11:07,940 --> 00:11:09,060
Anyway, well done.

242
00:11:09,180 --> 00:11:10,780
You did a marvelous job out there.

243
00:11:11,060 --> 00:11:11,940
Much appreciated.

244
00:11:13,860 --> 00:11:14,860
I just...

245
00:11:14,860 --> 00:11:15,380
Can I...

246
00:11:15,380 --> 00:11:17,080
Can I maybe ask you something, sir?

247
00:11:18,340 --> 00:11:18,860
Sure.

248
00:11:18,980 --> 00:11:19,460
What is it?

249
00:11:19,840 --> 00:11:21,440
I was just wondering...

250
00:11:22,160 --> 00:11:23,720
How can I become the Wizard King?

251
00:11:23,720 --> 00:11:27,900
I see.

252
00:11:28,060 --> 00:11:30,660
So the two of you are looking to become the Wizard King, are you?

253
00:11:31,020 --> 00:11:33,740
Not surprising, given that you are magic knights.

254
00:11:34,200 --> 00:11:38,120
You two must realize how rude it is to ask a question like that so directly.

255
00:11:38,700 --> 00:11:39,320
Now listen.

256
00:11:39,720 --> 00:11:43,460
The Wizard King must be of noble heart and have the implicit trust of all of his people...

257
00:11:43,460 --> 00:11:44,300
No, Klaus.

258
00:11:48,260 --> 00:11:49,680
It's about results.

259
00:11:49,680 --> 00:11:54,560
A noble heart alone cannot protect anyone.

260
00:11:55,100 --> 00:11:57,660
And the trust of the people is earned, not granted.

261
00:11:58,540 --> 00:12:01,640
You want to know what you need to do to gain the title of Wizard King?

262
00:12:02,140 --> 00:12:03,180
Get results.

263
00:12:03,740 --> 00:12:05,120
Prove that you're the strongest.

264
00:12:06,700 --> 00:12:08,000
Do what it takes.

265
00:12:08,640 --> 00:12:10,200
Devote yourself to getting results.

266
00:12:10,460 --> 00:12:11,360
That's all there is.

267
00:12:13,660 --> 00:12:17,420
Anyone who's not capable of that cannot hope to stand at the summit.

268
00:12:17,420 --> 00:12:20,360
Exactly what I wanted to hear.

269
00:12:21,720 --> 00:12:23,040
Not bad, William.

270
00:12:23,300 --> 00:12:23,580
Yummy.

271
00:12:23,900 --> 00:12:25,740
I like the look in your newbie's eyes.

272
00:12:28,380 --> 00:12:31,980
Now I hope you're ready for something special,

273
00:12:32,100 --> 00:12:35,380
because today we've gathered those knights with an exceptional number of stars

274
00:12:35,380 --> 00:12:37,280
for the Distinguished Service Ceremony.

275
00:12:37,780 --> 00:12:39,060
The dis... what now?

276
00:12:39,320 --> 00:12:41,000
The Distinguished Service Ceremony.

277
00:12:41,600 --> 00:12:45,760
We give awards and commendations to those who have performed extraordinarily well.

278
00:12:45,760 --> 00:12:49,980
I would appreciate it if you would join us for it.

279
00:12:59,640 --> 00:13:02,540
This Distinguished Service Ceremony sounds fancy.

280
00:13:02,680 --> 00:13:03,800
I wonder what it's going to be like.

281
00:13:04,280 --> 00:13:05,100
Why us?

282
00:13:05,280 --> 00:13:07,020
I have a bad feeling about this.

283
00:13:07,540 --> 00:13:09,700
I hadn't expected this turn of events.

284
00:13:09,700 --> 00:13:15,160
Here we are.

285
00:13:17,440 --> 00:13:21,140
The question is, can you achieve greater results than these knights have?

286
00:13:21,140 --> 00:13:37,380
All right.

287
00:13:37,820 --> 00:13:40,560
Let the Distinguished Service Ceremony begin.

288
00:13:40,560 --> 00:13:46,740
The Clover Kingdom's Magic Knights are given ranks based upon the caliber of their performance.

289
00:13:47,420 --> 00:13:52,800
With the Wizard King at the top, the ranks are divided into five, from first through fifth class.

290
00:13:53,980 --> 00:13:56,320
Knights gain rank through exemplary performance.

291
00:13:56,900 --> 00:14:01,160
They must obtain the required number of stars before the annual Distinguished Service Ceremony,

292
00:14:01,520 --> 00:14:04,000
when the Wizard King will bestow new ranks accordingly.

293
00:14:04,000 --> 00:14:11,080
With a total of seven stars, from the Crimson Lion King squad, Leopold Vermillion, step forward.

294
00:14:11,820 --> 00:14:15,800
I hereby bestow upon you the rank of Intermediate Magic Knight, second class.

295
00:14:18,160 --> 00:14:23,680
Like your brother, Captain of the Crimson Lion Kings, your use of flame magic can be a bit overwhelming.

296
00:14:24,680 --> 00:14:26,940
You may want to consider toning it down a little.

297
00:14:26,940 --> 00:14:31,880
There's no room for mercy when you're fighting against evil, sir.

298
00:14:32,820 --> 00:14:37,340
Next, with a total of six stars, from the Blue Rose Knights, Sol Maron.

299
00:14:38,780 --> 00:14:42,260
I grant you the rank of Intermediate Magic Knight, third class.

300
00:14:43,180 --> 00:14:48,020
Your vitality, a match for any man's, is amazing, as is your unique earth magic.

301
00:14:48,440 --> 00:14:50,520
But perhaps you have a bit too much freedom.

302
00:14:50,720 --> 00:14:52,820
The only person who can tie me down is Charlotte.

303
00:14:53,620 --> 00:14:55,180
I mean, my captain.

304
00:14:55,180 --> 00:15:01,340
Now, with a total of six stars, hailing from the Silver Eagles, I call Solid Silva.

305
00:15:02,040 --> 00:15:05,300
I grant you the rank of Intermediate Magic Knight, third class.

306
00:15:05,700 --> 00:15:07,960
You exhibit great skill in controlling your magic,

307
00:15:08,200 --> 00:15:12,640
but it would be better if you could work with those around you rather than showing off your own powers.

308
00:15:13,300 --> 00:15:15,220
I'll keep that in mind going forward.

309
00:15:15,720 --> 00:15:20,720
With a total of nine stars, from the Silver Eagles, is Nebra Silva.

310
00:15:20,720 --> 00:15:24,840
I grant you the rank of Senior Magic Knight, fifth class.

311
00:15:25,360 --> 00:15:29,200
The illusions that you create with your mist magic are truly incredible.

312
00:15:29,980 --> 00:15:33,860
But you have a habit of using them to toy with your foe more than necessary.

313
00:15:34,140 --> 00:15:35,320
It may backfire someday.

314
00:15:35,780 --> 00:15:37,040
Thank you for the advice.

315
00:15:37,320 --> 00:15:38,320
I'll take it to heart.

316
00:15:38,960 --> 00:15:40,800
With a total of seven stars.

317
00:15:40,800 --> 00:15:43,980
Hailing from the Golden Dawn, Hammond Cassius.

318
00:15:44,920 --> 00:15:48,580
I hereby grant you the rank of Intermediate Magic Knight, second class.

319
00:15:49,020 --> 00:15:51,580
Looking at you, one wouldn't think you'd wield glass magic.

320
00:15:51,920 --> 00:15:53,900
I imagine that often confuses your enemies.

321
00:15:54,520 --> 00:15:55,560
Yes, sir, it does.

322
00:15:55,660 --> 00:15:56,160
Thank you.

323
00:15:56,160 --> 00:16:00,820
Next, with a total of eight stars.

324
00:16:01,200 --> 00:16:03,700
Also from the Golden Dawn, Shirin Tiam.

325
00:16:04,880 --> 00:16:07,960
I grant you the rank of Intermediate Magic Knight, first class.

326
00:16:08,280 --> 00:16:12,020
Behind your eloquent magic is a reticent mage who rarely speaks his own mind.

327
00:16:12,520 --> 00:16:15,480
I encourage you to make your thoughts and opinions known more often.

328
00:16:16,560 --> 00:16:17,000
Sir.

329
00:16:18,000 --> 00:16:20,600
And now with a total of eleven stars.

330
00:16:20,980 --> 00:16:23,740
From the Golden Dawn, Alecdora Sandler.

331
00:16:23,740 --> 00:16:28,300
I grant you the rank of Senior Magic Knight, fourth class.

332
00:16:28,800 --> 00:16:32,180
I commend you for both your flexible magic and your diligent demeanor.

333
00:16:32,840 --> 00:16:35,520
However, you might consider relaxing occasionally.

334
00:16:36,360 --> 00:16:37,760
Welcome words, sir. Thank you.

335
00:16:38,580 --> 00:16:42,680
Your efforts have helped bring the Golden Dawn's total to 71 stars.

336
00:16:42,880 --> 00:16:44,060
A commanding lead.

337
00:16:44,540 --> 00:16:47,200
The rest of you will have to work hard not to be left behind.

338
00:16:48,600 --> 00:16:50,600
Well, that concludes the formal bit.

339
00:16:50,600 --> 00:16:54,020
We've also prepared a simple banquet to celebrate the occasion.

340
00:16:54,220 --> 00:16:55,660
So please enjoy yourselves.

341
00:16:56,160 --> 00:16:59,560
And you may not have noticed, but I invited some special guests.

342
00:17:00,960 --> 00:17:03,380
I hope you'll mix and mingle with them as well.

343
00:17:05,180 --> 00:17:06,040
Pardon, sir.

344
00:17:09,660 --> 00:17:11,620
I'm sorry, but something's come up.

345
00:17:11,660 --> 00:17:12,840
You'll have to excuse me.

346
00:17:12,980 --> 00:17:14,240
Have an excellent time now.

347
00:17:14,240 --> 00:17:25,140
Their contempt is almost palpable.

348
00:17:25,720 --> 00:17:27,480
How are we supposed to enjoy this?

349
00:17:31,980 --> 00:17:33,060
Just look at them.

350
00:17:33,240 --> 00:17:35,900
Why would the Wizard King subject us to this kind of treatment?

351
00:17:36,760 --> 00:17:39,520
The man himself couldn't even stick around to witness it.

352
00:17:39,520 --> 00:17:44,000
What is this?

353
00:17:44,260 --> 00:17:48,940
I've never had anything like this.

354
00:17:49,000 --> 00:17:51,000
Though it doesn't seem to have affected him much.

355
00:17:51,420 --> 00:17:52,900
As unashamed as ever.

356
00:17:53,360 --> 00:17:54,620
I wouldn't say unashamed.

357
00:17:54,780 --> 00:17:55,960
More uncivilized.

358
00:17:56,140 --> 00:17:57,560
Uh, excuse me.

359
00:17:57,720 --> 00:17:58,760
I was thinking.

360
00:17:59,300 --> 00:18:01,260
If you don't mind, maybe I'd join you?

361
00:18:01,620 --> 00:18:02,780
Oh, sure, Mimosa.

362
00:18:03,180 --> 00:18:05,140
So you've been eyeing this meat too, huh?

363
00:18:05,140 --> 00:18:06,500
Oh, yes.

364
00:18:06,820 --> 00:18:07,980
It looks very delicious.

365
00:18:08,540 --> 00:18:10,060
Filthy gluttonous commoner.

366
00:18:10,980 --> 00:18:13,740
Why would the Wizard King invite such a vulgar guest?

367
00:18:14,140 --> 00:18:16,220
I can't sense any magic power in him.

368
00:18:16,520 --> 00:18:20,120
If he did clear that dungeon, I'm sure it was purely by luck.

369
00:18:20,380 --> 00:18:22,300
What a positively atrocious eater.

370
00:18:24,000 --> 00:18:26,380
It's much like having a rat in the throne room.

371
00:18:26,660 --> 00:18:28,160
His presence here is unnatural.

372
00:18:31,160 --> 00:18:31,640
Huh?

373
00:18:32,240 --> 00:18:34,180
You guys really don't play your punches, huh?

374
00:18:34,180 --> 00:18:36,200
Oh, well, nothing I'm not used to.

375
00:18:37,400 --> 00:18:39,480
It doesn't even seem to bother him!

376
00:18:39,800 --> 00:18:43,260
If I remember correctly, you've got a commoner in your squad, too.

377
00:18:44,240 --> 00:18:48,020
Everyone thinks he's a big deal because of his four-leaf clover grimoire.

378
00:18:48,500 --> 00:18:50,600
But he's a commoner through and through.

379
00:18:52,720 --> 00:18:55,220
They might have pulled off the dungeon-crawling mission.

380
00:18:55,580 --> 00:18:58,060
But I have no doubt I would have done a better job.

381
00:18:59,460 --> 00:19:02,860
Well, Crimson Lion Cub, aren't you full of yourself?

382
00:19:02,860 --> 00:19:07,100
His work may be subpar, but it's not as if we expect much of a commoner.

383
00:19:07,560 --> 00:19:08,920
True, he's Golden Dawn.

384
00:19:09,540 --> 00:19:13,220
But it is we nobles who embody the ideals of our squad and captain.

385
00:19:14,560 --> 00:19:16,340
Now, with all due respect...

386
00:19:16,340 --> 00:19:17,600
And what about you, Klaus?

387
00:19:17,600 --> 00:19:22,720
Klaus, a man of your caliber ought to be ashamed to be seen in the company of those commoners.

388
00:19:23,300 --> 00:19:30,060
As for you, Mimosa, I hear you were promptly wounded in the dungeon and removed yourself from the front lines.

389
00:19:30,760 --> 00:19:34,360
Your ineptitude is making Royal House Vermillion a laughingstock.

390
00:19:34,360 --> 00:19:36,980
I-I'm sorry, I didn't mean to.

391
00:19:37,820 --> 00:19:39,840
No! She performed admirably!

392
00:19:42,100 --> 00:19:43,340
Come, Alecdora.

393
00:19:44,100 --> 00:19:46,820
We all know who the most inept person here is.

394
00:19:48,080 --> 00:19:50,300
And it's not poor little Mimosa.

395
00:19:51,160 --> 00:19:52,540
Right, Noel?

396
00:19:52,540 --> 00:20:00,420
Why, Solid? Why would you do that?

397
00:20:00,920 --> 00:20:02,280
Enter your own sister!

398
00:20:03,280 --> 00:20:05,860
You can't even control your magic properly.

399
00:20:06,580 --> 00:20:08,620
Could there be any greater disgrace than you?

400
00:20:08,880 --> 00:20:12,500
You were as good as banished from House Silva for being an abject failure.

401
00:20:13,160 --> 00:20:16,500
How dare you come waltzing back into the noble realm as if you belong?

402
00:20:17,220 --> 00:20:18,860
Nabra, please stop this!

403
00:20:20,540 --> 00:20:26,240
You let a single success go to your head, and now you've come here to sully the Silva name with your presence.

404
00:20:27,660 --> 00:20:29,780
But... we were invited!

405
00:20:30,700 --> 00:20:33,220
This is no place for a pathetic creature like you.

406
00:20:33,880 --> 00:20:34,700
Now leave.

407
00:20:35,620 --> 00:20:37,620
Wasn't killing our mother enough?

408
00:20:37,620 --> 00:20:39,620
Gah!

409
00:20:46,500 --> 00:20:50,360
You don't need to run away from people like this, Noelle.

410
00:20:50,760 --> 00:20:52,620
But... I...

411
00:20:52,620 --> 00:21:02,520
You were invited here by the Wizard King, so I figured you had to be pretty amazing.

412
00:21:03,020 --> 00:21:05,700
But you're just like all the rest of them, aren't you?

413
00:21:06,980 --> 00:21:10,680
Commoner. Rat. Disgrace. Failure.

414
00:21:11,160 --> 00:21:13,660
Do you think I care if I fit in with you people?

415
00:21:13,660 --> 00:21:16,620
No! Watch! Because I will!

416
00:21:18,820 --> 00:21:20,880
That's enough out of you, little rat.

417
00:21:21,300 --> 00:21:24,300
We will not be spoken to in such a manner by your kind.

418
00:21:24,500 --> 00:21:25,140
Be quiet.

419
00:21:26,800 --> 00:21:28,060
Not a chance!

420
00:21:28,780 --> 00:21:29,660
How dare you!

421
00:21:29,700 --> 00:21:32,300
Now you better listen up, because I wasn't done talking!

422
00:21:32,860 --> 00:21:35,160
I'm gonna get results like no one has before!

423
00:21:35,580 --> 00:21:38,480
I'll do whatever it takes to become the Wizard King!

424
00:21:38,940 --> 00:21:40,780
And prove you wrong!

425
00:21:43,660 --> 00:21:44,300
, but...

426
00:21:44,300 --> 00:21:48,660
Amo!

427
00:21:49,340 --> 00:21:49,820
Eight!

428
00:21:50,300 --> 00:21:50,540
Eight!

429
00:21:50,540 --> 00:21:50,980
Nine!

430
00:21:50,980 --> 00:21:51,580
Ten!

431
00:21:52,180 --> 00:21:52,820
Three!

432
00:21:55,580 --> 00:21:55,660
Five!

433
00:21:58,120 --> 00:21:58,600
Nine!

434
00:21:59,900 --> 00:22:00,480
rat!

435
00:22:00,820 --> 00:22:01,480
Ten!

436
00:22:02,040 --> 00:22:02,540
Ten!

437
00:22:02,560 --> 00:22:02,740
Zero!

438
00:22:02,740 --> 00:22:02,960
One!

439
00:22:04,380 --> 00:22:05,200
Eight!

440
00:22:09,260 --> 00:22:10,200
Ten!

441
00:22:10,940 --> 00:22:11,560
One!

442
00:22:11,820 --> 00:22:12,620
Ten!

443
00:22:12,620 --> 00:22:17,620
消えそうな光でも 闇を照らす力が

444
00:22:17,620 --> 00:22:22,620
繋がって 時の流れを変える

445
00:22:24,620 --> 00:22:27,620
色褪せない場所に

446
00:22:31,620 --> 00:22:36,620
終わらない夢を掴むため 進むべき道があるなら

447
00:22:36,620 --> 00:22:41,620
Do you wanna drive? Do you wanna drive? このままどこを待ってても

448
00:22:41,620 --> 00:22:46,620
僕の命が終わるまで どんな痛みも受け入れよう

449
00:22:46,620 --> 00:22:48,620
We can drive now! We can drive now!

450
00:22:48,620 --> 00:22:55,620
たとえ明日が見えなくても 声にならない

451
00:22:55,620 --> 00:23:01,620
想いを抱いて 叫び続ける in my heart

452
00:23:06,620 --> 00:23:15,620
プリテッド

453
00:23:15,620 --> 00:23:17,620
クロークエスト

454
00:23:18,620 --> 00:23:24,620
月曜 月曜 マジエス

455
00:23:24,620 --> 00:23:26,620
僕が初めを聞いた

456
00:23:27,620 --> 00:23:29,620
同 twenties、フレーズな Hmm

457
00:23:29,620 --> 00:23:33,620
メ撃ちの体がある

458
00:23:33,620 --> 00:23:38,740
Asta, you're being incredibly rude to your Magic Knight superiors.

459
00:23:38,940 --> 00:23:40,460
Now hurry up and say you're sorry.

460
00:23:40,740 --> 00:23:42,220
I'll apologize along with you.

461
00:23:42,440 --> 00:23:45,500
Black Clover, page 21, Capital Riot.

462
00:23:45,800 --> 00:23:49,120
My magic is learning to accept some brat calling me four-eyes.

